e container's center column (31.5): c' = 63 - c.\nV's region mirrored: row 40: 63-31=32 \u2192 32; row 41: 63-32=31, 63-31=32 \u2192 31-32; row 42: 63-32=31, 63-31=32, 63-30=33 \u2192 31-33; row 43: 63-32=31, 63-31=32, 63-30=33, 63-29=34 \u2192 31-34.\nSo VL's region \u2248 rows 40-43: 32, 31-32, 31-33, 31-34.\nThe remaining white cells: (40,32), (41,30), (41,33), (42,29), (42,33), (42,34), (43,28), (43,33), (43,34), (43,35).\nVL's region \u2229 white: (40,32) \u2713, (41,33)? VL's row 41 = 31-32 \u2192 no. (42,33) \u2713, (42,34)? VL's row 42 = 31-33 \u2192 no. (43,33) \u2713, (43,34) \u2713.\nSo VL paints at most 4 of the remaining 10: (40,32), (42,33), (43,33), (43,34).\nV paints (40,32)? V's row 40 = 31 \u2192 no. V's region \u2229 white = \u2205 (computed earlier).\nSo even adding VL, the coverage is: V (10) + VL (~10) + H (50) + LD (25) + RD (55).\nNewly covered cells: (40,32), (42,33), (43,33), (43,34) [from VL], and V's 10 (already counted).\nStill uncovered: (41,30), (41,33), (42,29), (42,34), (43,28), (43,35) \u2014 6 cells!\nHmm. Are there other new states? By symmetry: what about RD-U? Tested: no change. H-U/H-D: no change.\nWhat about LEFT from V? Tested: no change. RIGHT from VL? Untested! Let's test VL-R.\nAlso, what about DOWN from H... no change. UP from V... goes to RD.\nWhat about LEFT from VL? Untested. RIGHT from VL? Untested.\nLet's test VL-R and VL-L.\nAlso, there might be a 5th orientation: a diamond on the right side... no, RD is a diamond.\nState list: H (horizontal rectangle), LD (left diamond), RD (right diamond), V (right vertical), VL (left vertical).\nWhat about a \"horizontal but lower\" state? Or a diamond below the container?\nLet's test VL-R and VL-L (2 actions).", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": true}, {"label": "ASSISTANT", "content": "Found a 5th state: VL (left vertical, rows 33\u201344, cols 18\u201324). Testing its horizontal transitions.", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL CALL: python", "content": "